5	@@ -35,6 +35,10 @@ and this project adheres to [Semantic Versioning](https://semver.org/).
6	 
7	 ### Fixed
8	 
9	+- Treat a recognized concurrent-ref rejection as skipped work when a fresh target advertisement confirms the exact desired hash. Other refusals remain unchanged, and later ref batches still run.
10	+
11	+- Read target refs before source refs so a concurrent sync that finishes between discovery reads cannot become the expected-old baseline for rewinding a branch or pruning a newly created ref from an older source snapshot.
12	+
13	 - Preserve source-read errors when closing bootstrap observation, including `io.ErrUnexpectedEOF`; a truncated source is reported as `observer_failed`, not expected `observer_interrupted`. Intentional partial closure is unchanged. ([#120](https://github.com/entireio/git-sync/pull/120))
14	 
15	 - At source EOF, bootstrap upload guards enforce actual bytes without projection or the batching safety margin. Final bytes returned together with EOF remain subject to the byte limit, and diagnostic counters retain their observed values. ([#120](https://github.com/entireio/git-sync/pull/120))
